/-- **The harmonic energy of nine distinct points of the unit sphere of `ℝ⁴` is at least `35 / 2`**: the first
part of the theorem T8 (`S3N9.Minimum9`, stated in `S3N9/Statement.lean`). -/
theorem minimum9 : S3N9.Minimum9 :=
  S3N9.minimum9_of claims54_excl exclL0 claimsRing_excl claimsSel_excl leavesVR_excl innerOK

/-- The lower bound with the contacts in the case of equality: the input of the proof of uniqueness. -/
theorem lower_and_contacts {x : Fin 9 → Fin 4 → ℝ} (hx : S3N9.OnSphere x) (hinj : Function.Injective x) :
    35 / 2 ≤ S3N9.energy x ∧ (S3N9.energy x ≤ 35 / 2 → ∃ μ : Equiv.Perm (Fin 9),
      S3N9.InLeaf S3N9.Leaf.I (S3N9.pt x ∘ μ) ∧ S3N9.Contacts (S3N9.pt x ∘ μ)) :=
  S3N9.lower_and_contacts claims54_excl exclL0 claimsRing_excl claimsSel_excl leavesVR_excl innerOK hx hinj

/-- **The theorem for nine points on the three-sphere** (T8, `S3N9.Harmonic9` of `S3N9/Statement.lean`): the
regular pentagon with the orthogonal square consists of nine distinct points of the unit sphere of `ℝ⁴` and has
the harmonic energy `35 / 2`; every configuration of nine distinct points of the sphere has an energy of at
least `35 / 2`; and a configuration with the energy `35 / 2` arises from it by an orthogonal map and a
relabelling of the points. -/
theorem harmonic9 : S3N9.Harmonic9 :=
  S3N9.harmonic9_of claims54_excl exclL0 claimsRing_excl claimsSel_excl leavesVR_excl innerOK

